module Sable.Core

// Concurrency's one core type (docs/02 §2.7): Sable.Concurrency's channels,
// groups and sleeping are written over it. Its members' bodies are the
// compiler's ('@intrinsic'): a task is a class holding the runtime's handle,
// the body to run and, once run, its result, laid out per result type, and
// the runtime schedules it (SilGen.Tasks.cs).

/// A task running concurrently, and, once it finishes, its result.
public class Task<Success> {
    /// Made by 'spawn' alone: a task is its body, queued.
    private init() { }

    /// The body, queued to run as a task of its own; the task, to await.
    @intrinsic
    public static fn spawn<T>(_ body: async () -> T) -> Task<T>

    /// The task's result, waiting for it to finish.
    @intrinsic
    public var value: Success { async get }

    /// Lets every task queued run before this one goes on.
    @intrinsic
    public static async fn `yield`()

    /// Waits at least this many nanoseconds, off the run queue: every other
    /// task runs meanwhile, and the program waits only when none can. A
    /// task cancelled while asleep wakes at once.
    @intrinsic
    public static async fn sleep(nanoseconds: Int)

    /// Asks the task to stop. Cancelling is cooperative: the task goes on
    /// until it asks 'Task.isCancelled()' and returns early itself, but a
    /// sleep it is in, or starts, ends at once. Cancelling a task that has
    /// finished, or cancelling twice, does nothing.
    @intrinsic
    public fn cancel()

    /// Whether the running task has been cancelled.
    @intrinsic
    public static fn isCancelled() -> Bool
}
